id: pm-swarm-assignment-brief
title: Give each swarm worker a budgeted assignment brief
description: "Project the selected item into one budgeted, fenced work brief for the assigned agent."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-11-21T03:19:44.094Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-21T15:47:46.630Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: The current owner and exact swarm generation are required in shared and Git trackers.; Only the requested item is disclosed and JSON and TOON fit the SDK-estimated token budget with exact disclosure counts.; Concurrent real worker processes verify assignment isolation and stale-fence refusal.; README documents a measured before and after from a synthetic tracker and package gates pass.
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-21T03:20:13.864Z",codex-sol,"Synthetic baseline (25 tasks, core 2026.11.18): orient plus full item costs 2691 SDK-estimated JSON tokens, or 2645 with item-scoped orient. A fixed field get costs 157 but excludes recent comments and has no owner fence. Existing stale reclaim recovered one item; its 342-token receiver packet omitted acceptance criteria, and scoped core handoff context cost 849. Existing footprint planning excluded all 8 contenders with zero observed overlap admissions; fair scheduling also excluded the single skill mismatch. Implement a one-item SDK projection using the existing owner and generation, whole fields or rows, exact omission counts and the SDK estimator in both native formats. Preserve selection and add concurrent real worker acceptance."
  "2026-11-21T03:27:50.053Z",codex-sol,"Measured one assignment before handoff on the 25-task fixture: brief 479 estimated JSON tokens at a 512 cap, down 2212 (82.2%) from orient plus full get and 525 (52.3%) from explicit fields including comments. Scoped orient plus full get was 2645. The same explicit fields refused at 512. The brief retains the criteria, footprint and eight progress comments, with 11 comment rows omitted. The unchanged selection receipt was 772 tokens."
  "2026-11-21T03:27:53.544Z",codex-sol,"The new read uses the SDK guard or the exact bound provider client, checks active owner and decimal generation, and sizes complete JSON and TOON using the SDK estimator. Fenced Git transfers work without changing legacy Git acquisition or sync behavior. Follow-ups are pm-swarm-reclaim-digest and pm-swarm-git-fenced-acquisition. The PM-linked test ran 3/3 with no skips. Full coverage is running."
  "2026-11-21T03:28:22.271Z",codex-sol,"Ranked gaps per worker loop: assignment context first (2212 estimated tokens saved from orient plus full get), richer recovery second (one extra criteria and artifact lookup avoided on each stale replacement), footprint prediction third (zero incremental prevention on the measured known overlaps). In a separate concurrent two-item fixture sharing one file, core 2026.11.18 claim-next assigned both items to different agents and existing swarm next assigned only one. The package already supplies cross-item footprint admission and skill-aware fairness."
  "2026-11-21T03:40:02.207Z",codex-sol,"Source commit 11823d6 includes the brief and all three tracker document/history pairs. The real packed extension on core 2026.11.18 reproduced 479 JSON tokens and measured 474 TOON tokens against 1796 for orient plus full get, saving 1322 (73.6%). The field-selected TOON read took 1016. Typecheck and lint passed on Node 26; the new module reached 100/100/100/100 in focused coverage. The full coverage gate continues on Node 26."
  "2026-11-21T04:31:27.125Z",codex-sol,"The stock Node 26 coverage process hit its one-hour watchdog after all three exhaustive close crash cohorts passed. Completed-prefix V8 data was preserved. The remaining 60 test files are running under the same Node runtime and test concurrency, starting with the first interrupted file. The package source inventory and all four thresholds will be applied to the combined coverage data."
  "2026-11-21T05:02:14.892Z",codex-sol,"Final local evidence on Node 26.13.0: npm run typecheck, npm run lint, npm run docstring and npm run duplication passed. PM-linked node --test test/assignment-brief.test.ts passed 3/3 and node --test test/privacy-invocation.test.ts passed 10/10 after updating the sweep to 23 command variants. All 94 test files were accounted for across the completed coverage prefix and resumed suffix, including all references to touched files. The single-process npm run coverage reached its 3600-second watchdog with no assertion failures before cancellation. The completed prefix and resumed V8 data passed the package checker for all 43 source files: 4637/4637 statements and lines, 3319/3319 branches and 365/365 functions. Fetching origin tags, regenerating the full changelog and checking it passed."
  "2026-11-21T15:40:38.950Z",codex-sol,"Review thread PRRT_kwDOVLY-P866TpHg on PR #96. Apply the shared private-path scanner and SDK secret guard to brief output, keep the identity privacy refusal, and record privacy withholding without exposing the withheld content. Verify against real tracker fixtures."
  "2026-11-21T15:44:31.844Z",codex-sol,"Privacy omission is field-wide, including collection rows. Budget counts continue for otherwise safe fields. Exercise identity refusals, private progress and acceptance text, stored and normalized footprints, and SDK credential findings in a linked test and custom status. Confirm JSON and TOON fit with omission markers and preserve the durable tracker snapshot."
  "2026-11-21T15:47:46.629Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck, lint, docstring and duplication gates passed. Focused c8 measured 100% statements, branches, functions and lines for src/assignment-brief.ts with five passing tracker tests. The JSON and TOON receipts retained public context and a numeric budget omission while withholding all detected fields. Package-wide coverage and command references are still running."
